    "name": "Le Concorde",
    "notes": "Hôtel Le Concorde (1974), Grande Allée: a 26-floor concrete slab tower whose Grande Allée side falls in terraces like a ski jump, under the revolving restaurant L’Astral. Façade frame on Cours du Général-De Montcalm, Grande Allée (−along) to Wilfrid-Laurier (+along). From an aerial photo looking south-west. A 13 m podium on the whole footprint, showing either side of the 22 m-deep tower; the tower is two slabs either side of a recessed darker channel, centred on the restaurant; ten terraces from 72 m down to 18 m toward Grande Allée; the restaurant where OSM maps it (76–91 m): a glazed ring, a concrete band and a smaller drum. Replaces OSM’s restaurant part.",
